---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--  Logging
--  (HEADER=VALUE)
--  Logging values are stored in the swCardEventLogTable, each OID entry represents each slot
--  position.  The indexing of the table works using the log header string. For example if the
--  header is "FAULT", the index OID starts with the length of the header ie 5, followed by the
--  ASCII values for each letter 70 65 85 76 84.
--  Index for "FAULT" .5.70.65.85.76.84
--  To OID for FAULT on slot 12 for swCardEventLogTable is 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.12. 5.  70.65.85.76.84
--                                                         |-------base-----------|Slt|Len|-F--A--U--L--T-|
--  An SNMP GET on this OID will return the Log value associated with FAULT for slot 12 eg "NONE" (FAULT=NONE)
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: SN
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .2.83.78
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.2.83.78
-- Vary			: NO
--
-- Value(s)		: xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
--				: 
-- Comments		: Serial Number   Runtime string  
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: EDH
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .3.69.68.72
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.3.69.68.72
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: NONE              The unit is not locked to the input signal
--				: FAIL              EDH errors have been found on the input signal
--              : OK                No EDH errors found on the input signal
--              : RESET             EDH statistics have been reset
-- Comments		: 
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: MSG
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .3.77.83.71
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.3.77.83.71
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: UNIT PRESENT
--				: UNIT LOST
-- Comments		: 
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: STD
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .3.83.84.68
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.3.83.84.68
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: STDERR            Input signal standard not recognized or no signal
--				: UNKNOWN           Not a selected input standard
--              : 525               Input standard 525
--              : 625               Input standard 625
-- Comments		: 
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: STD1
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .4.83.84.68.49
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.4.83.84.68.49
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: ERR               Not a selected input standard Input 1
--				: 525               Input 1 standard 525
--              : 625               Input 1 standard 625
-- Comments		: 
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: STD2
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .4.83.84.68.50
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.4.83.84.68.50
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: ERR               Not a selected input standard Input 2
--				: 525               Input 2 standard 525
--              : 625               Input 2 standard 625
-- Comments		: 
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
